---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import ReadmeGenerator from '../../components/ReadmeGenerator.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="AI README Generator"
  description="Describe your project and instantly generate a clean, structured README.md — bring your own Anthropic API key."
>
  <ReadmeGenerator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Skip the blank-page README problem</h2>
  <p>
    Every project needs a README, but writing one from scratch is easy to
    put off. This tool generates a solid first draft — Overview, Features,
    Installation, Usage, License — that you can edit and refine rather than
    starting from nothing.
  </p>

  <h2>How to use this</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Enter your API key (stored only in your browser).</li>
    <li>Fill in project name, description, and tech stack.</li>
    <li>Generate, then copy and refine the result in your editor.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>AI README Generator FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Will this know my actual code?</strong> No — it generates based
    on the description you provide, not your codebase. For best results, be
    specific about what your project does and how it's used.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Can I regenerate just one section?</strong> Not currently —
    regenerating produces a full new draft; copy the sections you want to
    keep before regenerating if you've already edited part of the output.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Does it include a license section automatically?</strong> Yes —
    mention your preferred license (e.g. MIT) in the description, and it
    will include a matching License section in the generated README.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
